## Platform Quick Reference

Use this table as an initial orientation, not as a fixed rule. Platform algorithms, audience behavior, and effective posting frequency can change. Adapt recommendations to the target audience, market, account performance, and available resources.

| Platform | Best For | Suggested Starting Frequency | Key Formats |
|----------|----------|-----------|------------|
| LinkedIn | B2B, thought leadership, professional networking | 3–5 times/week | Carousels, stories, text posts |
| Twitter/X | Tech, real-time commentary, niche communities | Multiple posts/replies per day | Threads, short posts, commentary |
| Instagram | Visual brands, lifestyle, e-commerce | 1–2 feed posts/day plus Stories as appropriate | Reels, carousels, Stories |
| TikTok | Brand awareness, discovery, short-form video | 1–4 videos/day as a testing reference | Short-form vertical video |
| Facebook | Communities, local businesses, broad audiences | 1–2 posts/day as a starting reference | Groups, native video, discussion posts |

Do not recommend a frequency that exceeds the user's actual production capacity. Consistency and content quality should be considered alongside posting volume.

For detailed platform strategies, see `references/platforms.md`.

