## Content Calendar Structure

A content calendar connects content pillars, formats, publishing dates, channels, and objectives.

### Weekly Planning Template

| Day | LinkedIn | Twitter/X | Instagram |
|-----|----------|-----------|-----------|
| Monday | Industry insight | Thread | Carousel |
| Tuesday | Behind-the-scenes | Engagement | Story |
| Wednesday | Educational | Tips post | Reel |
| Thursday | Story post | Thread | Educational content |
| Friday | Opinion or discussion | Engagement | Story |

This is an example of a weekly structure, not a mandatory schedule. Select platforms based on the user's actual audience and resources.

### Batching Strategy (2–3 Hours Weekly)

1. Review content pillar topics.
2. Select ideas for the coming week.
3. Draft the core messages and hooks.
4. Adapt content to each platform.
5. Prepare visuals, captions, and CTAs.
6. Schedule content where appropriate.
7. Leave room for real-time engagement and timely topics.

Batching should reduce repetitive work without making content feel overly repetitive or disconnected from current events.

